{"id":"src/lib/pax/admin/api.ts","pkg":"src/lib/pax","kind":"module","lines":130,"commentLines":21,"header":["THE PAX ADMIN REQUESTS (step 64a). I use one handler for every operation the panel can ask; the route (src/app/api/pax/admin/route.ts) only brings the logged-in person and the database. The person comes from the LOGIN SESSION and from nowhere else: whatever the browser says about itself (a ticket, a name, a role) is ignored. I enforce the rules of who may do what here AND again inside the database transaction (store.ts), so the panel hiding a button is a courtesy, never the protection. logged out -> 401 logged in, no authority (not the HOD, not authorised) -> 403 for everything except \"me\" the HOD of C&IT (SUPERADMIN_TICKETS) -> everything an authorised executive -> entries (list, add, modify, delete) and the history; NOT authorising or revoking, NOT the list of authorised people The server looks up the executive to authorise in the people directory (a typed name is never trusted): only an executive (ticket 4xxxxx) exists for this purpose."],"symbols":[{"name":"ApiContext","kind":"interface","exported":true,"line":20,"generics":"","extends":"","doc":[],"members":[{"kind":"field","name":"actor","line":22,"type":"Actor | null","optional":false,"readonly":false,"doc":["The logged-in person (ticket and name from the session and the people directory), or null."]},{"kind":"field","name":"db","line":23,"type":"PaxDb","optional":false,"readonly":false,"doc":[]},{"kind":"field","name":"findByName","line":24,"type":"(name: string) => Promise<EmployeeResult[]>","optional":false,"readonly":false,"doc":[]},{"kind":"field","name":"findByTicket","line":25,"type":"(ticket: string) => Promise<EmployeeResult[]>","optional":false,"readonly":false,"doc":[]}],"id":"456774a610-ApiContext","usedBy":[]},{"name":"ApiReply","kind":"interface","exported":true,"line":27,"generics":"","extends":"","doc":[],"members":[{"kind":"field","name":"status","line":27,"type":"number","optional"